window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>He needs a wife to silence his father. She needs a break from the spotlight.</p> <p>Millie Greer thought she was destined for Broadway, until a cruel director crushed her dreams over a few extra pounds. Now, hiding from the stage that once defined her life, she’s found solace behind the microphone, recording for an erotic stories app.</p> <p>Ezra Miller is a big-hearted middle school teacher, worn down by his father’s constant pressure and his own string of romantic misfortunes. When he’s met with an unexpected family member, Ezra’s only option is to find a “wife”—and fast. Who better to play the role than a trained actress?</p> <p>What begins as a convenient arrangement quickly spirals as the line between make-believe and reality blurs. When hearts get tangled, Ezra and Millie must decide if their fake relationship is for the show—or if love might be the real deal after all.</p> <p>Packed with laugh-out-loud humor, witty banter, and a whole lot of spice, <i>For the Show</i> is a heartwarming story about finding family, self-love, and realizing that sometimes, the best roles are the ones we never expected to play.</p> <p><i>For the Show</i> is the second book in the All for Love interconnected standalone series but can be listened to on its own.</p>"; 
